# Store and deliver every file exactly as it is, with no line-ending conversion.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf = true, which would make Git normalise CRLF to LF inside the
# repository and convert it back on checkout. On Windows the round trip is invisible, but a clone
# on Linux or macOS would receive different bytes, and the MD5 values recorded in
# output/MANIFEST_output.csv would no longer match the files. The datasets and the pattern files
# are experimental evidence, so byte equality matters more than tidy line endings.
* -text
